Professor Chen: Welcome to the research methods seminar. Today we're reviewing experimental design.

Maya: I've been reading about between-subjects versus within-subjects designs.

Jordan: Can you explain when you'd choose one over the other?

Professor Chen: Between-subjects avoids order effects but requires more participants. Within-subjects controls for individual differences but risks carryover. [face=smile]

Maya: So a mixed design could give you the best of both? [face=awe]

Professor Chen: In many cases, yes. The key is matching your design to your research question.
